// Validate a flow.
//
// Read-only pre-publish check. Returns `valid` (= no `error` issue), `issues[]` — the single list to
// act on, each with `code`, `severity` (`error`/`warning`), `stepId` (the node to fix; absent for
// whole-flow problems), optional `handle` (the branch) and `detail` — plus `stepCount`,
// `hasEntryTrigger` and the legacy `danglingTargets`, `orphanStepIds`, `incompleteChannelSteps` (same
// findings, still returned). ERRORS: `missingEntryTrigger`; `danglingTarget` (output points at a
// removed step); `incompleteChannelStep` (channel node missing its sender, or an email with an empty
// body — `detail` = reason); `whatsappTemplateNotApproved` (`detail` = template status);
// `brokenReference` (`detail` = what no longer exists: tag, stage, pipeline, offer, list,
// whatsappNumber, whatsappTemplate); `senderNumberUnavailable` (the WhatsApp number pinned in the node
// — fixed, or the attendant fallback — is `archived`, deactivated or has automations disabled;
// `detail` says which). WARNINGS: `unreachableStep`; `stepWithoutNext` (ends there — often
// intended); `emptyConditionalBranch`; `triggerWithoutScope` (`detail` = event whose required scope is
// unset); `variableOutsideTriggerContext` (a message uses a variable its trigger does not provide,
// `detail` = the variable, e.g. the webinar magic link; it would render empty). Warnings never make
// `valid` false. Not checked statically: numbers taken from the trigger context (`numberStrategy:
// 'context'`). Note that `flows_activate` itself only refuses a missing entry trigger and incomplete
// channel nodes — the other `error` codes are NOT blocked at activation but the sends will fail, so
// fix them first. A step targeting the trigger step (infinite loop) is rejected at write time by
// `flows_step_connect`/`flows_step_create`, so this check does not look for it. To test with a real
// contact instead, see `flows_test_run_start`. Also returned: `triggerWithoutOutput` — the trigger
// connects to nothing while other steps exist, so the automation fires and does nothing.
// `orphanStepIds` and `triggerWithoutOutput` are what YOU must clear before telling the user the flow
// is ready (fix them with `flows_graph_apply`), even though neither makes `valid` false.
//
// Calls GET /flows/validate.
func (s *FlowsService) Validate(ctx context.Context, params FlowsValidateParams, opts ...Option) (*FlowsValidateOutput, error) {
	var out FlowsValidateOutput
	if err := s.client.do(ctx, "GET", "/flows/validate", params.values(), nil, &out, opts); err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return &out, nil
}

